{"Unconditionally calling `pipeline.fetch_state` when reading `installation_id` from the query string can raise if the state isn't set - should retrieve query param first and only call fetch_state when missing": 0.4867108166217804, "Direct indexing into `integration.metadata[\"sender\"][\"login\"]` risks a runtime error if metadata is missing or malformed - should use safer lookup like `integration.metadata.get(\"sender\", {}).get(\"login\")`": 0.8658000826835632, "Catching bare `Exception` when parsing the OAuth token response may hide unexpected failures - should narrow the except to specific parsing/IO errors or at least log unexpected exceptions": 0.622406005859375, "Inconsistent capitalization of \"GitHub\" in the short error message - `error_short` uses \"Github\" but other messages use \"GitHub\"": 0.06507382541894913, "Hard-coding the `responses.calls` index (responses.calls[2]) is brittle with the new OAuth requests - should iterate over responses.calls and select by URL/method instead": 0.20580577850341797, "In `GitHubInstallation.dispatch`, the new `Integration.objects.get(external_id=installation_id, status=ObjectStatus.ACTIVE)` block will cause fresh installations (where the webhook hasn't yet created the Integration row) to be treated as an invalid installation request - should fall back to `pipeline.next_step()` when integration does not yet exist": 0.170308455824852, "The new `error()` helper returns a generic 'Invalid installation request.' message for several distinct failure modes - should differentiate error_short/error_long messages to make troubleshooting easier": 0.15662313997745514, "The new helper named `error` is very generic and shadows Python's built-in idiom - should rename to something domain-specific like `render_installation_error`": 0.016156122088432312, "The OAuth token exchange and parsing logic in `OAuthLoginView.dispatch` largely duplicates what exists in `OAuth2CallbackView` - should refactor into a shared helper": 0.06091759726405144}